@startuml ngram-trie-storage
' N-gram key encoding: words are interned to u64 vocabulary indices, LEB128-varint
' encoded, and each byte is carried as a Latin-1 char so any char-keyed trie can store
' the key. Index 0 is reserved so a varint never collides with the \x00 metadata prefix.
' Render: plantuml -tsvg docs/diagrams/ngram-trie-storage.puml
' Source of truth for Figure 1 in docs/components/ngram/trie-storage.md
skinparam backgroundColor #FAFAFA
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultTextAlignment center
skinparam linetype ortho
skinparam rectangle {
  FontColor white
  FontStyle bold
  BorderColor #263238
  roundCorner 12
}
skinparam ArrowColor #37474F
skinparam ArrowFontColor #37474F
title N-gram key encoding — words ⇒ varint ⇒ trie key

legend top right
  |= Color |= Concept |
  |<#1565C0>     | Statistical LM core |
  |<#00838F>     | Storage / persistence |
  |<#C62828>     | Deprecated / unsafe |
  |<#546E7A>     | Tokens / result |
endlegend

rectangle "**n-gram tokens**\n[ the · quick · brown ]" as toks #546E7A

rectangle "**Legacy encoding** (deprecated)\nthe|quick|brown\n⚠ a token containing '|' corrupts the split" as legacy #C62828

rectangle "**Vocabulary ARTrie**\ninsert(w) → u64  (idempotent, lock-free)\nthe → 1 · quick → 2 · brown → 3\nFIRST_VALID_INDEX = 1" as vocab #00838F
rectangle "**LEB128 varint**\n7 payload bits/byte, high bit = continue\n1 → [0x01]   128 → [0x80,0x01]" as varint #1565C0
rectangle "**Latin-1 carrier**\nbyte 0xNN → char U+00NN\nkey = ⟨U+0001, U+0002, U+0003⟩" as latin1 #1565C0

rectangle "**VocabularyIndexedDictionary<D>**\nsplit → encode → delegate\nOOV reads never mutate the vocabulary" as vid #00838F
rectangle "**Backend trie D**\nDynamicDawgChar · PathMapDictionary\nSharedCharARTrie · DoubleArrayTrieChar" as backend #00838F
rectangle "**NgramEntry**\ncount · continuation_count\nunique_continuations  (all atomic)" as entry #1565C0

rectangle "**\\x00 METADATA_PREFIX**\nreserved subtree — hidden by\nMetadataFilteringZipper" as meta #546E7A

toks --> legacy : v0.2 (do not use)
toks --> vocab : v0.3+
vocab --> varint
varint --> latin1
latin1 --> vid
vid --> backend : get / insert
backend --> entry : value
backend --> meta : sibling subtree

note right of vocab #E3F2FD
  Index 0 is never assigned: varint(0) = 0x00,
  which would alias the metadata prefix and be
  filtered out of every traversal.
end note

note right of varint #E3F2FD
  Zipf's law pays here: the ~127 most frequent
  words each cost a single byte, so a typical
  5-gram key is ~5-8 bytes.
end note

@enduml
